# GroceryHub Sprint 1 — Revised Architecture Plan (v2)

> This is a ground-up revision of the Sprint 1 architecture. Every change from v1 is documented with rationale. Self-critiques of previous design decisions are called out explicitly.

---

## 1. Critical Self-Review of v1 Architecture

Before presenting the updated design, here are the flaws I identified in my own previous proposal:

| v1 Decision | Problem | v2 Fix |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Named models `Order` / `OrderItem` | Tightly couples the domain to "grocery orders." Breaks when receipts come from pharmacies, fuel stations, restaurants, or utilities. | Renamed to `Receipt` / `ReceiptItem` — a universal purchase abstraction. |
| Upload endpoint returned a file path and implicitly assumed receipt creation would follow | Couples file upload to receipt lifecycle. In reality, upload → AI parse → user preview → save is a multi-step pipeline. | Upload endpoint is **fire-and-forget**: saves file, returns file metadata. No Receipt is created. |
| Single flat `uploads/` directory | A single directory with millions of files causes filesystem performance degradation (inode exhaustion, slow `ls`, slow lookups on ext4/NTFS). | Date-partitioned structure: `uploads/2026/07/uuid.pdf`. |
| No `status` field on Receipt | Cannot track receipt lifecycle (uploaded → processing → processed → failed). Critical for async AI pipelines. | Added `status` enum field with defined state machine. |
| No `store_type` field | Cannot categorize or filter by purchase category. Limits future analytics. | Added `store_type` enum. |
| No `currency` field | Assumes single currency. Breaks for international users or multi-currency households. | Added `currency` field (default `INR`). |
| No `raw_ai_response` field | Nowhere to store the raw Gemini API output for debugging, auditing, or re-parsing. | Added `raw_ai_response` JSON column. |
| No `metadata` JSON field | No extensibility mechanism for future fields without schema migrations. | Added `metadata` JSON column. |
| No `storage_provider` field | When migrating from local disk to S3/GCS, existing records lose track of where their files live. | Added `storage_provider` field (`LOCAL` for Sprint 1). |
| `StorageService` naming | Too generic. Collides conceptually with database storage or cloud storage configuration. | Renamed to `FileStorageService` — explicitly about file I/O. |

