### Architectural Layers (Clean Architecture)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Transport Layer (HTTP)                                         │
│  app/api/v1/endpoints/ — Route handlers, request parsing,       │
│  response formatting, HTTP status codes                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Application Layer (Use Cases / Services)                       │
│  app/services/ — Business logic, orchestration, validation      │
│  ReceiptService, FileStorageService                             │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Domain Layer (Entities)                                        │
│  app/models/ — SQLAlchemy ORM models (Receipt, ReceiptItem)     │
│  app/schemas/ — Pydantic v2 DTOs (Create, Read, Response)       │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Infrastructure Layer                                           │
│  app/database/ — Async engine, sessions, migrations             │
│  app/core/ — Config, logging, exception handling                │
│  app/utils/ — File validation, path helpers                     │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Why Clean Architecture?** Each layer depends only on layers below it. The Transport Layer never touches SQLAlchemy directly. The Service Layer never imports FastAPI types. This makes it possible to:
- Swap FastAPI for gRPC without touching services.
- Swap SQLite for PostgreSQL without touching routes.
- Add background workers (Celery/ARQ) that call the same services without HTTP.

