## 6. Enum Definitions

All enums are defined in `app/core/enums.py` and used by both SQLAlchemy models and Pydantic schemas:

```python
class StoreType(str, Enum):
    INSTANT_GROCERY = "INSTANT_GROCERY"     # Blinkit, Zepto, Swiggy Instamart
    SUPERMARKET = "SUPERMARKET"             # BigBasket, DMart, More
    PHARMACY = "PHARMACY"                   # Apollo, PharmEasy, 1mg
    RESTAURANT = "RESTAURANT"              # Swiggy, Zomato
    ECOMMERCE = "ECOMMERCE"               # Amazon, Flipkart
    FUEL = "FUEL"                          # Petrol, diesel, EV charging
    UTILITY = "UTILITY"                    # Electricity, water, gas
    OTHER = "OTHER"

class ReceiptStatus(str, Enum):
    UPLOADED = "UPLOADED"
    PROCESSING = "PROCESSING"
    PROCESSED = "PROCESSED"
    FAILED = "FAILED"

class StorageProvider(str, Enum):
    LOCAL = "LOCAL"
    S3 = "S3"
    GCS = "GCS"

class Currency(str, Enum):
    INR = "INR"
    USD = "USD"
    EUR = "EUR"
    GBP = "GBP"
```

**Why `str, Enum`?** Inheriting from `str` ensures the enum serializes to its string value in JSON responses and Pydantic schemas without custom serializers.

