## 9. Additional Improvements (Beyond User Requirements)

### 9.1 TimestampMixin

```python
class TimestampMixin:
    created_at = mapped_column(DateTime(timezone=True), server_default=func.now())
    updated_at = mapped_column(DateTime(timezone=True), server_default=func.now(), onupdate=func.now())
```

**Why?** Every future model (User, FlatGroup, Budget, PantryItem) will need timestamps. A mixin eliminates duplication and enforces consistency.

### 9.2 Paginated Response Schema

```python
class PaginatedResponse(BaseModel, Generic[T]):
    items: list[T]
    total: int
    skip: int
    limit: int
```

**Why?** A generic paginated wrapper standardizes list endpoint responses across all future resources. Clients can build pagination UI components once.

### 9.3 Request ID Middleware

Every request gets a unique `X-Request-ID` header (UUID), logged with every log line. This enables end-to-end request tracing in production.

### 9.4 Application Factory Pattern (`create_app()`)

Instead of a module-level `app = FastAPI()`, we use a factory function:

```python
def create_app() -> FastAPI:
    app = FastAPI(...)
    app.include_router(...)
    register_exception_handlers(app)
    return app
```

**Why?** Enables creating isolated app instances for testing, prevents import side effects, and supports multiple configurations (test vs. production).

